        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.724,
            0.382,
            0.744
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ready to Go Beyond"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.75,
            0.762,
            0.815
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Newton’s laws describe motion across an enormous range of scales, from everyday objects to planets and stars. They need modification only very close to massive objects, at extremely high speeds near the speed of light, and very small (atomic) scales."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.108,
            0.836,
            0.145,
            0.879
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 13,
              "bbox": [
                0.108,
                0.836,
                0.145,
                0.879
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_21_image_13.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.156,
            0.861,
            0.387,
            0.879
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The Quest Continues…"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.889,
            0.752,
            0.954
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In the real world, friction is always present whenever surfaces are in contact. Scientists have been trying to find ways to reduce friction between surfaces by using lubricants, coatings or texturing of surfaces, streamlining shapes of objects, and by using magnetic levitation."
            }
          ]
        }
